From: Marcus Ramberg <marcus.ramberg@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] input: rmi4: support OnePlus 6/6T aftermarket S3706B digitizers

Aftermarket OnePlus 6/6T (enchilada/fajita) replacement panels use a
Synaptics S3706B that (a) reports an unpopulated PDT (valid base addresses
but zero interrupt-count / function-number bytes), (b) issues an internal
reset partway through F01 configuration, briefly reporting "unconfigured",
and (c) does not expose usable F12 sensor dimensions until configured, so
rmi4 falls back to a 0..65535 coordinate range. Stock mainline aborts with:

  rmi4_i2c 12-0020: First PDT entry is empty and no backup values provided
  rmi4_f01 rmi4-00.fn01: Device was reset during configuration process, status: 0x1!
  probe with driver rmi4_f01 failed with error -22

and, once probing, reports touch over 0..65535 which is unusable.

Fixes:
 - Advertise "syna,rmi4-s3706b" so rmi_driver's fallback-PDT path is used,
   and correct rmi_s3706_fallback_pdt (bare decimal literals meant F34/F12
   compiled to 0x22/0x0c so the touch handler never bound; use the real
   function numbers F34=0x34, F01=0x01, F12=0x12).
 - Tolerate the "unconfigured" F01 status only for panels using that
   fallback PDT (pdt_fallback_size != 0); all other devices keep the
   original fatal behaviour.
 - Pin the coordinate range via syna,clip-* to the 1080x2340 panel.
--- a/drivers/input/rmi4/rmi_f01.c
+++ b/drivers/input/rmi4/rmi_f01.c
@@ -574,10 +574,27 @@
 	}
 
 	if (RMI_F01_STATUS_UNCONFIGURED(device_status)) {
-		dev_err(&fn->dev,
-			"Device was reset during configuration process, status: %#02x!\n",
-			RMI_F01_STATUS_CODE(device_status));
-		return -EINVAL;
+		/*
+		 * Aftermarket S3706B panels (identified by the fallback PDT
+		 * supplied via the "syna,rmi4-s3706b" compatible) issue an
+		 * internal reset while being configured and briefly report
+		 * "unconfigured"; they settle on their own once the host stops
+		 * re-configuring them, and the vendor driver ignores this
+		 * status. Their axis range comes from the syna,clip-* device-
+		 * tree properties, so it does not depend on the controller
+		 * being configured here. Tolerate the status for those panels
+		 * only; every other device still treats it as fatal.
+		 */
+		if (pdata->pdt_fallback_size) {
+			dev_warn(&fn->dev,
+				"Device reset during configuration (status %#02x); continuing.\n",
+				RMI_F01_STATUS_CODE(device_status));
+		} else {
+			dev_err(&fn->dev,
+				"Device was reset during configuration process, status: %#02x!\n",
+				RMI_F01_STATUS_CODE(device_status));
+			return -EINVAL;
+		}
 	}
 
 	dev_set_drvdata(&fn->dev, f01);
